{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Because they did not meet you with bread and water.</b> Rashi explained: on account of the counsel that they gave to cause you to sin. But this matter is not explicit in the verse, and the essence is missing from the text. Moreover, reason does not accept that two nations would be distanced merely because they did not greet them with bread. Rather, certainly the essence is that they caused them to sin. And this matter is clarified in the verse: the reason they did not greet them with bread and water was so that they would be hungry and thirsty from the fatigue of the journey, and through this they would inevitably eat from the sacrifices of their gods and drink from their wine-libations that accustom one to licentiousness, as is concluded in Sanhedrin (106a) — for anyone who is exhausted and weary does not examine carefully between forbidden and permitted, and eats and drinks from whatever is given to him. And the Holy One, blessed be He, knew their intention in this manner; therefore they were distanced. Hence it says: ״עַל דְּבַר אֲשֶׁר לֹא קִדְּמוּ״ — that is, on account of that hidden matter toward which they aimed by not greeting them. And even though the females were the primary ones in the harlotry, nevertheless the principal guilt hangs on the men, for it is their way to extend hospitality first, and the men began the corruption, and they compelled their daughters to commit harlotry. And for this reason the female children of Israel were spared in the war against Midian, for they erred in this judgment — that the distancing applied specifically to the males. And this explanation is more precious than what all the commentators have said on this, and all the difficulties they raised are resolved."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:13:17.330448649Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}